contract; do not hand-edit either one. Re-vendor with `git show
<commit>:contracts/settings/v1/<file>` from the server repo, update the commits
below, regenerate iosApp/iosApp/Networking/SettingKeys.generated.swift with the
server's generator at the same commit (`go run ./cmd/settingsgen -lang swift
-out <path>`), then run the SiloTests scheme —
SettingsConformanceTests fails when the fixture's manifest_revision, the
vendored manifest's revision, and the generated SettingKey.revision stop
agreeing, which is the whole point of carrying the pair rather than the
fixture alone.

